  "question": "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{dx}{2+\\cos x}$.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Use substitution $t=\\tan\\frac{x}{2}$.<br /><br />Then $\\cos x=\\frac{1-t^2}{1+t^2}$ and $dx=\\frac{2}{1+t^2}dt$.<br /><br />Substituting gives $\\int \\frac{2}{3+t^2}dt$.<br /><br />$=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)+C$.<br /><br />Replacing $t=\\tan\\frac{x}{2}$ gives the final answer.",
